chunks.explanation_md:
**Asset.** Its historical cost is updated to show, where applicable:

(a) **consumption** of part or all of the resource (**depreciation or amortisation**);
(b) **payments received** that extinguish part or all of the asset;
(c) events that make part or all of the cost **no longer recoverable** (**impairment**); and
(d) **accrual of interest** for any financing component.

**Liability.** Its historical cost is updated to show, where applicable:

(a) **fulfilment** of part or all of it (payments, or delivering goods);
(b) events that raise the value of the obligation until the liability becomes **onerous**, that is, the historical cost is no longer enough to show the obligation to fulfil it; and
(c) **accrual of interest** for any financing component.

**Amortised cost.** One way to apply historical cost to financial assets and liabilities is **amortised cost**. It reflects estimates of future cash flows **discounted at a rate set at initial recognition** (updated for variable rate instruments), and is updated for interest accrual, impairment of a financial asset, and receipts or payments.

questions.model_answer_md:
When fair value cannot be observed directly in an active market it is estimated using techniques, including **cash-flow-based techniques**. The technique reflects:

(a) **estimates of future cash flows**;
(b) possible **variations in the amount or timing** of those cash flows caused by uncertainty;
(c) the **time value of money**;
(d) the **price for bearing the uncertainty** (a risk premium or discount); and
(e) **other factors**, such as liquidity, if market participants would consider them.

Factors (b) and (d) include the risk that a counterparty fails to fulfil its liability (**credit risk**) or that the entity fails to fulfil its liability (**own credit risk**).

**Transaction costs.** Because fair value is not derived from the transaction price, it is **not increased by transaction costs incurred on acquiring** the asset, not decreased by those on incurring a liability, and does **not reflect transaction costs on ultimate disposal** or on transferring or settling a liability.

The measure reflects the assumptions of **market participants**, not the entity.
